A(('h1', S13))
A(('p', '13.1 Related passages. Read each in its own setting and keep it apart from these stories.'))
A(('bul', [
    'Luke 15:1–2: the drawing near and the murmuring that stand before the stories.',
    'Luke 5:29–32: another setting in which the Pharisees and scribes murmur against eating and drinking with publicans and sinners, with its own words from Jesus.',
    'Matthew 18:1–3, 10, 14–15: the question about greatness, the child, the words about “these little ones” and what follows the sheep.',
    'Matthew 18:11 and Luke 19:10: sentences about that which was lost, each standing in its own place and not part of the sheep and the coin.',
    'Matthew 10:5–7 and 15:24: Jesus’ words about “the lost sheep of the house of Israel,” spoken in other settings.',
    'Luke 4:43 and Matthew 4:17: what Jesus was sent to preach and what He preached.',
]))
A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Lost Son and the Elder Brother, the Unforgiving Servant and the Two Debtors are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. These stories make no use of their meanings, and they make none of these.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus tells of a man who loses one of a hundred sheep and goes after it until he finds it, and of a woman who loses one of ten pieces of silver and seeks it diligently till she finds it. Each finding ends in a calling together of friends and neighbours to rejoice, and Jesus says there is joy in heaven and in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner that repenteth. He names nothing else in the stories, and Matthew’s account of the sheep, told in another setting, closes with the Father’s will that one of these little ones should not perish.'))
A(('p', 'Write the synthesis in your own words in five to seven sentences. In it:'))
A(('bul', [
    'Tell the sheep and the coin in their order.',
    'State exactly what Jesus says in Luke 15:7 and 15:10 and nothing beyond it.',
    'Say plainly which parts of the stories Jesus does not identify.',
    'State what the comparisons say about a lost one that is sought and found.',
    'State when Jesus told them and what He was sent to preach, and one principle of conduct for today.',
    'End with one sentence naming what the passage does not say.',
]))
A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names joy in heaven, the angels of God, one sinner that repenteth and ninety and nine just persons which need no repentance, and nothing more. No identity for the man, the sheep, the woman, the coin, the friends or the neighbours. No symbol carried in from another parable. Seeking, finding, rejoicing and repenting are actions in stories, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is neither the sheep nor the coin. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))
